      "writtenOn": "2024-08-29T22:08:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is really a question about how `argparse` handles options. If there are no `-` characters in the option, you can provide the value to `-g` with spaces, like you would any other option. However, if the value for `-g` has a `-` character, you must use an equals sign `\u003d` to clarify that the option is not for `cros debug` itself. If there are spaces in the option, you must use quotes. I\u0027ve clarified this here.",
      "parentUuid": "a41604bf_939cb1a6",
      "revId": "e59fe3c1e006cd1a864e12a30533e1c15a81ee79",
